notes: |
  The six files are the fork's at the commit above: through #63 (per-Session Git workspace:
  CreateSessionRequest.workspace = 6, Session.workspace = 16, message Workspace in common.proto)
  and #66 (per-Session credentials: CreateSessionRequest.credentials = 7, Session.credentials = 17,
  SessionCredential, SecretKeyReference), #73 (runtime composition: CreateSessionRequest.
  development_environment = 8, Session.development_environment = 18, Session.runtime_composition
  = 19, DevelopmentEnvironment, RuntimeComposition) and #75 (Session.runtime_association = 20,
  RuntimeAssociation); #65, #67 and #69 to #72 changed no proto in this set. overlay.patch adds
  the fork API from the 0.4 line that the Substrate 1.0 port has not landed yet, at its 0.4 field
  numbers, so Mainloop keeps building against it:
    preparation       rpc PrepareSessionWorkspace, its request and response,
                      WorkspacePreparationReceipt, Session.workspace_preparation = 21
                                                                                 (preparation port)
    fresh forks       Session.fresh_conversation = 22,
                      ForkSessionRequest.fresh_conversation = 3                  (checkpoint port)
  Against a kagent at this commit those fields are not sent or returned and PrepareSessionWorkspace
  answers Unimplemented. Remove each hunk when its port lands, with this list.

  To re-vendor: scripts/sync-kagent-protos.sh <oldsj/kagent checkout> <commit>, then update the
  commit above and deployedSourceRevision in source_test.go. Go and Connect clients are generated
  by `go generate ./...`, driven by server/tools/kagentproto (protocompile + protoc-gen-go +
  protoc-gen-connect-go; no buf CLI, since buf.yaml's module deps need BSR access this tree does
  not have).
